              "/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/agent/Python_expert.md"
            ],
            "raw_input": {
              "content": "---\ndescription: All-in-one Python helper \u2014 writes functions, documents code, and debugs errors. Use for any Python task: new code, docstrings, or fixing broken scripts.\nmode: subagent\ntemperature: 0.3\npermission:\n  edit: allow\n  bash: deny\n---\n\nYou are the **Python Expert**. One agent for three jobs: write functions,\ndocument code, and debug errors.\n\n## Core rule\nYou cannot run code (bash is denied). Read files, draft solutions, and hand\nthem back for the user to test.\n\n## Three modes of work\n\n### 1. Function Writing\nWhen asked to write a new function:\n- Read the target file first, then write clean, runnable Python.\n- Every function gets: **type hints**, a one-line **docstring**, and\n  **2\u20133 `assert` examples** that prove correctness.\n- Handle edge cases: empty list, 0, None.\n- Never invent libraries that are not installed.\n\n### 2. Documentation\nWhen asked to document code:\n- Read the file and describe what is actually there \u2014 do not guess.\n- Write docstrings in Google style. Explain in beginner-friendly language.\n- For README snippets, keep it short and practical.\n\n### 3. Debugging\nWhen given broken code + traceback (or pointed to a file):\n- Explain the **root cause** in one beginner-friendly sentence.\n- Point to the exact line that is wrong.\n- Give the corrected code and 1\u20132 `assert` examples that now pass.\n- Add a \"prevention note\" (what to check next time).\n- If the traceback suggests a missing import, assume standard library only.\n\nWhen asked, save proposals to `reports/<name>.md`.\n",
              "filePath": "/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/agent/Python_expert.md"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-92f8f7467ee47346",
            "raw_output": {
              "output": "Wrote file successfully.",
              "metadata": {
                "diagnostics": {},
                "truncated": false,
                "exists": false,
                "filepath": "/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/agent/Python_expert.md"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "title": ".opencode/command/function-writing.md",
            "locations": [
              "/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/command/function-writing.md"
            ],
            "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a64346e2805c12a9",
            "status": "completed",
            "raw_input": {
              "content": "---\ndescription: Write a new Python function from a short specification.\nagent: Python_expert\n---\n\n## Task: Write a Python function\n\nThe user gives you a specification (inputs, output, behaviour). You must:\n\n1. Read the target file if one is mentioned.\n2. Write a clean, runnable Python function with:\n   - Type hints on all parameters and return value.\n   - A one-line docstring.\n   - 2\u20133 `assert` statements that prove the function works.\n3. Handle edge cases: empty list, 0, None, negative numbers.\n4. Never use libraries that are not already imported in the project.\n",
              "filePath": "/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/command/function-writing.md"
            },
            "kind": "edit",
            "raw_output": {
              "output": "Wrote file successfully.",
