            "title": ".opencode/command/doc-writing.md",
            "kind": "edit",
            "raw_input": {
              "content": "---\ndescription: Add docstrings and documentation to existing Python code.\nagent: Python_expert\n---\n\n## Task: Document Python code\n\nThe user gives you a file or a code snippet. You must:\n\n1. Read the code carefully \u2014 document what is actually there, do not guess.\n2. Write a Google-style docstring for every function.\n3. Explain the purpose of each function in beginner-friendly language.\n4. Keep it short: one sentence of \"why\", then `Args` / `Returns` / `Raises`.\n5. Do not change any logic \u2014 only add or improve documentation.\n",
              "filePath": "/home/jovyan/Intro_to_AI_HW2/.opencode/command/doc-writing.md"
            },
            "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-957976be0f079f35"
