              "content": "---\ndescription: Add docstrings and documentation to existing Python code.\nagent: Python_expert\n---\n\n## Task: Document Python code\n\nThe user gives you a file path or pastes a code snippet.\n\n1. Read the code carefully \u2014 document only what is actually there. Do not guess or embellish.\n2. Add a Google-style docstring to every function that does not already have one.\n3. Each docstring includes:\n   - One sentence explaining *why* the function exists (its purpose).\n   - `Args:` \u2014 each parameter with its type and meaning.\n   - `Returns:` \u2014 the return type and what it means.\n   - `Raises:` \u2014 any exceptions the function may raise (if obvious from the code).\n4. Do not change any logic \u2014 only add or improve comments and docstrings.\n5. Use beginner-friendly language throughout.\n"
            },
            "kind": "edit",
