      "id": "34ec38b5-7f76-4626-9856-c2978752ac8a",
      "body": "how to restart you?",
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "st158862"
    },
    {
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "To restart me (the opencode session), you have a few options:\n\n1. **Exit and relaunch** \u2014 close the terminal and run `opencode` again in your project directory. This starts a fresh session.\n\n2. **Start a new chat** \u2014 in the opencode UI, create a new conversation (usually a \"New Chat\" button or `/new` command). Your old conversation is saved as a `.chat` file.\n\n3. **Clear context within the same session** \u2014 use `/help` inside opencode to see available commands (there may be a `/clear` or similar).\n\nYour current chat history lives in `Main_chat.chat` and `Main.chat` \u2014 those files persist, but a new session won't load them automatically.",
